# --------------------------------------------------
# Ignore list for Prettier.
#
# This file lists files and patterns that should
# be ignored by Prettier.
#
# The Prettier CLI uses .gitignore and .prettierignore
# from the directory where it is run. For configuration,
# Prettier climbs up from the formatted file until it finds
# a configuration file or reaches the home directory.
#
# The Prettier VS Code extension uses prettier.ignorePath,
# which points to one ignore file by default. If a file is
# ignored by .gitignore but not by .prettierignore, the
# extension may still format it on save.
# --------------------------------------------------

# Changelog is generated by semantic-release
**/CHANGELOG.md

# Tool-owned files
**/.gitattributes
**/*-lock.json
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/*.lock
# Native dependency graphs are checksum-addressed and owned by mise
.mise/locks/**
# Upstream schema bundles have checksum-verified bytes owned by schemas:update
schemas/*.schema.json
!schemas/devcontainer.schema.json
!schemas/sources.schema.json
schemas/sources.lock.json
# Preserve collected notices and checksum-addressed inventories
/licenses/**
!/licenses/README.md
!/licenses/sources.json
!/schemas/license-sources.schema.json

# Preserve the two-space separator in sha256sum manifests
**/*.sha256

# Husky internals
.husky/_/**

# Project rules
# Shared checks visit projects separately to respect their local ignore files
/projects/*/
/.local-work/
**/node_modules/**
**/dist/**

# Preserve generator-owned output and disposable tool caches
**/.generated/**
**/.cache/**
